+\subsection{VRAM Budget Enforcement}
+\label{sec:vrambudget}
+
+A per-model VRAM footprint table (\texttt{config.MODEL\_VRAM\_MIB}), populated from
+measured peak values rather than published estimates, backs a pre-flight
+\texttt{ensure\_vram\_available()} check called before every model load and before
+the \texttt{--ollama-polish} pass. Rather than allowing a CUDA out-of-memory error
+to surface mid-inference --- a failure mode that is hard to diagnose because it
+depends on which other processes already hold VRAM --- the check compares the
+requested model's measured footprint against currently free VRAM and raises a
+clean, actionable \texttt{RuntimeError} naming the offending model and the shortfall
+before any GPU memory is allocated. The \texttt{--ollama-polish} pass sequences this
+check between pipeline stages: translate $\to$ unload translator $\to$ pre-flight
+check $\to$ load polish model $\to$ polish per paragraph, ensuring the two models
+are never required to coexist in VRAM.
+
