+\subsection{July 2026 Inference Optimization Pass}
+\label{sec:optpass}
+
+Three code-level optimizations were applied to the translation pipeline in
+July~2026, each validated with a $\pm$0.3 BLEU-parity gate against the
+pre-change baseline before being accepted:
+
+\begin{enumerate}
+  \item \textbf{Batched sentence translation.} The pipeline previously issued one
+        model call per sentence for HF-backed models (MiLMMT, Seamless). Routing all
+        sentences through the existing \texttt{translate\_sentences()} batch path
+        (already used by the CT2 backend) gave the largest single gain: NLLB-600M
+        \NLLBBEFORECHS{}$\to$2{,}108\,chars/s, MiLMMT-46-1B 74$\to$326\,chars/s,
+        Seamless-medium 73$\to$300\,chars/s, at BLEU parity (NLLB $\Delta$0.0,
+        Seamless $\Delta$0.0, MiLMMT $\Delta{-}$0.3: 65.0$\to$64.7, an expected
+        left-padded-batch-generation effect on causal LMs, not a regression). The
+        original single-sentence loop is retained behind a \texttt{--no-batch} flag
+        for future A/B measurement. (SDPA does not apply to the CT2 backend, and
+        length-sorted batching's effect on NLLB is within session-to-session
+        measurement noise; the cumulative NLLB figure in Table~\ref{tab:optpass},
+        2{,}072\,chars/s, is consistent with this batching-only figure of 2{,}108
+        within that noise band, not a regression from the later steps.)
+
+  \item \textbf{SDPA attention with a per-architecture fallback.} PyTorch's scaled
+        dot-product attention (SDPA) kernel replaces eager attention for
+        architectures that support it, giving MiLMMT (Gemma3-based)
+        326$\to$399\,chars/s (+22\%) at BLEU~64.8 (chrF~79.4), passing the gate
+        against the 64.7 batched baseline. This could not be applied uniformly:
+        T5-based MADLAD-400 raises \texttt{ValueError} on
+        \texttt{attn\_implementation="sdpa"} in transformers~5.4.0
+        (\texttt{T5PreTrainedModel.\_supports\_sdpa=False}), so the shared
+        attention-resolver helper takes a per-architecture \texttt{fallback}
+        parameter (MADLAD $\to$ eager, Gemma3-family $\to$ SDPA). A
+        \texttt{flash-attn}~\cite{dao2022flashattention} build remains unavailable
+        on sm\_120/WSL2, so SDPA is the effective ceiling for this hardware.
+
+  \item \textbf{Length-sorted batching with order restoration.} Sorting inputs by
+        token length before batching reduces padding waste; an index-scatter step
+        restores original sentence order before postprocessing. BLEU parity is the
+        load-bearing correctness proof here (an order bug would silently mis-align
+        translations with source sentences): NLLB~55.27, MiLMMT~65.24, Seamless~67.00,
+        all at or above their respective baselines.
+\end{enumerate}
+
+Table~\ref{tab:optpass} reports the cumulative effect of all three optimizations,
+measured translate-only, warm cache, on the FLORES-200 90-sentence devtest.
+
+\begin{table}[htbp]
+\caption{Phase-1 Cumulative Speedup (Translate-Only, Warm Cache).}
+\label{tab:optpass}
+\centering
