+
+\textbf{Measurement pitfall: load time vs.\ translate time.} The original
+benchmark harness started its timer before \texttt{with translator:} entered,
+so model load --- including cold-page-cache disk reads of up to 5\,GB for the
+largest model --- was counted as translation time. Load time is also not
+comparable across runs for reasons unrelated to code: a warm page cache halves it
+(Seamless-medium: 96.0\,s cold vs.\ 50.6\,s warm, identical code). The fix reports
+\texttt{Load} and \texttt{Translate} as separate columns (Table~\ref{tab:throughput});
+only the translate-only figure is attributable to the optimizations in this section.
+
+\textbf{Single-run speed noise.} Repeated, identical-code MiLMMT runs in one
+session spanned 146--375\,chars/s, driven by host load rather than cache warming.
+Single-run throughput deltas under roughly 2$\times$ are not attributable to a code
+change on this shared, non-isolated development machine; BLEU/chrF at the
+$\pm$0.3 gate is used for correctness, and multi-run medians (not single closeout
+runs) should be used for any future speed claim beyond this paper's reported figures.
